%% End-to-end claim lifecycle - simulated. Acknowledgment != payment.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Claims Specialist
    participant API as Next.js /api/v1 + Server Actions
    participant CL as Claim svc
    participant RE as Rule engine
    participant EDI as EDI svc
    participant PR as Local processor (state machine)
    participant TR as Trace/Event svc
    participant RM as Remittance svc
    participant DB as Postgres (RLS)

    U->>API: Create 837P/837I draft
    API->>CL: validate tenant + persist (organization_id)
    CL->>DB: INSERT claim (status=Draft)
    U->>API: Validate claim
    API->>RE: universal + claim-type + payer edits
    RE-->>API: pass (all 10) / fail -> Validation Failed
    U->>API: Approve + Submit
    API->>EDI: generate scoped X12, preserve raw payload
    EDI->>DB: INSERT edi_transactions + edi_payloads (ISA/GS/ST ctrl #s, hashes)
    API->>PR: enqueue processing_job (idempotency_key)
    PR->>TR: TA1 Accepted (envelope received)
    PR->>TR: 999 Accepted (syntax OK)
    PR->>TR: 277CA Accepted for adjudication
    Note over PR,TR: Rejection would stop the claim HERE (pre-adjudication)
    PR->>RE: adjudication rules (payer_test_profile)
    alt 8 of 10 - covered
        RE-->>PR: PAID
        PR->>RM: generate synthetic 835 + adjustments
        RM->>DB: remittances, remit_service_lines, claim_adjustments
        PR->>TR: 835 Received -> EFT Matched -> Posted
    else 2 of 10 - denied AFTER adjudication
        RE-->>PR: DENIED (auth missing / benefit exhausted)
        PR->>TR: Denied (CARC/RARC or SIM code + rule_id + next action)
        Note over PR: No EFT deposit is matched for denials
    end
    U->>API: Open Transaction Trace
    API->>TR: full event graph (correlation_id)
    TR-->>U: every checkpoint, rejection vs denial kept separate
